          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>The Rediscovery of Mendel's Work</strong><br>\nMendel's laws were rediscovered independently by three scientists: Hugo de Vries, Carl Correns, and Erich von Tschermak in 1900. The significance of Mendel's findings was finally recognized, and he was posthumously credited with the discoveries.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Modern Genetics</strong><br>\nMendel's principles of heredity became the foundation for modern genetics. They have informed the development of new fields, including molecular biology, evolutionary biology, and genetic engineering.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mendel's Legacy and Memory</strong><br>\nToday, Gregor Mendel is celebrated as a pioneer in genetics. His birthplace and the monastery where he worked have become centers for education and tribute to his scientific contributions. Mendel's meticulous methodology and innovative approach to science education continue to inspire students and researchers.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
